@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "koroneiki"

Feature: Koroneiki Contact Role API Permissioning
	Testing Koroneiki Contact Role API Permissioning functionality.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the permissions for a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role" set for a non permissioned user
	* I tear down the contact roles on koroneiki with the following names
	| Default Account Customer Role  |
	| Optional Account Customer Role |

Scenario: Create contact role attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles that are attempted to get created by non permissioned users should not get created.

	Given I attempt to create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role"

Scenario: View contact role attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should not be viewable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Update contact role attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles that are attempted to get updated by non permissioned users should not get updated.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I attempt to update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Delete contact role attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should not be removable by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I attempt to delete a contact role on koroneiki with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Set contact role permissions attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should not be able to have their permissions set by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I attempt to set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: Unset contact role permissions attempt by non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should not be able to have their permissions unset by non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to unset the following permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" for a permissioned user as a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values as a permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role" and the following values as a permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |

Scenario: View contact role as permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should be viewable by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values as a permissioned user
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |

Scenario: Update contact role as permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should be able to be updated by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	And I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values as a permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |

Scenario: Delete contact role as permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should be removable by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Delete | true |
	And I delete a contact role on koroneiki with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a permissioned user
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role"

Scenario: Set contact role permissions by permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact role permissions should be able to have their permissions set by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Permissions | true |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values as a permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role" and the following values as a permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |

Scenario: Unset contact role permissions by permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact role permissions should be able to have their permissions unset by permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| Permissions | true |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user as a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" for a permissioned user as a permissioned user
	| Update | true |
	| View   | true |
	And I attempt to update a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values as a non permissioned user
	| Description | This is the optional customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Optional Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                                |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" and the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Optional Account Customer Role"
	And I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user

Scenario: View contact role attempt by newly non permissioned user
	Koroneiki account contact roles should not be viewable by newly non permissioned users.

	Given I create a contact role on koroneiki with the following values
	| Description | This is the default customer role for accounts |
	| Name        | Default Account Customer Role                  |
	| Type        | Account Customer                               |
	And I set the permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" to have the following values for a non permissioned user
	| View | true |
	And I unset the following permissions for the contact role "Default Account Customer Role" for a permissioned user
	| View | true |
	Then I should not be able to view a koroneiki contact role with the name "Default Account Customer Role" as a non permissioned user

